---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { site } from '../../content';
const path = "/guides";
const title = "Shopify email operator guides";
const desc = "Find operating guides for Shopify email selection, implementation, migration, permissions, cost and measurement.";
const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "Which guide comes first?",
    "answer": "Start with the immediate decision or incident, then follow its dependencies. Permission and sending defects need attention before expanding affected promotional audiences."
  },
  {
    "question": "Do these pages replace the internal runbook?",
    "answer": "Keep current store settings, ownership, exceptions and evidence in your own runbook. Link the guides for supporting procedure."
  },
  {
    "question": "Are merchant outcomes reported here?",
    "answer": "The exercises on this hub are proposals. They do not establish performed tests, vendor rankings or guaranteed financial results."
  }
];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="container py-16">
    <a class="link" href="/guides">Operator guides</a>
    <h1 class="hero-title mt-5 max-w-5xl">Choose a guide from the decision in front of you</h1>
    <p class="mt-7 max-w-3xl text-xl leading-9 text-[#4a2d17]">Find operating guides for Shopify email selection, implementation, migration, permissions, cost and measurement.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="container pb-12 grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-2" aria-label="All operator guides">
    <a class="card" href="/guides/selection-framework"><h2 class="text-2xl font-black">Selection framework</h2><p class="mt-3">Write requirements and evidence for a shortlist.</p></a>
    <a class="card" href="/guides/implementation-plan"><h2 class="text-2xl font-black">Implementation plan</h2><p class="mt-3">Sequence releases by data and operating dependencies.</p></a>
    <a class="card" href="/guides/migration"><h2 class="text-2xl font-black">Migration</h2><p class="mt-3">Transfer permissions, history and live sending ownership.</p></a>
    <a class="card" href="/guides/pricing-models"><h2 class="text-2xl font-black">Pricing models</h2><p class="mt-3">Compare quotes at actual contact and sending usage.</p></a>
    <a class="card" href="/guides/segmentation"><h2 class="text-2xl font-black">Segmentation</h2><p class="mt-3">Define audience membership and exclusion behavior.</p></a>
    <a class="card" href="/guides/deliverability"><h2 class="text-2xl font-black">Deliverability</h2><p class="mt-3">Diagnose sender and receiver signals.</p></a>
    <a class="card" href="/guides/discount-discipline"><h2 class="text-2xl font-black">Discount discipline</h2><p class="mt-3">Govern promises, code eligibility and contribution.</p></a>
    <a class="card" href="/guides/consent-compliance"><h2 class="text-2xl font-black">Consent and compliance</h2><p class="mt-3">Review channel, purpose and evidence of permission.</p></a>
    <a class="card" href="/guides/revenue-attribution"><h2 class="text-2xl font-black">Revenue attribution</h2><p class="mt-3">Separate reporting credit from causal impact.</p></a>
    <a class="card" href="/guides/flow-collision-prevention"><h2 class="text-2xl font-black">Flow collision prevention</h2><p class="mt-3">Resolve overlapping journeys and pending sends.</p></a>
  </section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl"><h2>Triage an active incident</h2><p>If messages are reaching withdrawn contacts, pause the affected promotional path and trace permission propagation with the consent guide. If a shopper receives conflicting offers, inspect pending sends with the collision guide. If a provider rejects or delays delivery, use the deliverability guide. Record the symptom and affected scope before considering a platform replacement.</p></div></section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl"><h2>Evaluate or renew a platform</h2><p>Start with selection and pricing. Write the required customer journeys, data dependencies, maintenance owner and commercial constraints. Ask finalists to demonstrate the same operations and provide comparable quotes. Read app reviews and comparisons as research inputs; this hub does not establish a universal platform winner or certify vendor capabilities.</p></div></section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl"><h2>Build a new program</h2><p>Use implementation to choose a bounded release, then the relevant use-case playbook for its message logic. Bring permission and sender setup into the release plan before enrollment. Add collision review as soon as audiences can overlap. Store-type guides help identify catalog and fulfillment exceptions rather than overriding customer permission.</p></div></section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl"><h2>Prepare a platform switch</h2><p>Use migration for the state-transfer and cutover plan, deliverability for sending diagnostics and consent for mapping exclusions. Decide who owns already-queued messages and new events during the move. Compare destination logic without allowing both equivalent flows to send. Keep rollback evidence before cancelling incumbent access.</p></div></section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl"><h2>Reconcile margin and reporting</h2><p>Read discount discipline alongside revenue attribution when dashboard sales grow but contribution is unclear. Preserve issued promises while reviewing future offers. Define refunds, discounts, cost inputs and reporting windows consistently. Use pricing models for platform expense; a lower subscription does not prove higher incremental profit.</p></div></section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl"><h2>Onboard a new operator</h2><p>Begin with the actual sender inventory, integration owners, permission map and incident history. Assign guides to gaps in that inventory rather than requiring a fixed reading calendar. Ask the new operator to explain one live journey, identify its pause action and trace a recent decision from source event to queue outcome.</p></div></section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl"><h2>Proposed handoff exercise</h2><p>Choose a test journey and write its expected branches before making changes. Have the incoming operator locate eligibility, change an exclusion in a non-sending copy, preview membership and restore the prior version. Retain questions and failures in the internal runbook. No completed merchant exercise or onboarding time saving is claimed here.</p></div></section>
  <section class="container pb-12"><div class="prose-shopify max-w-4xl"><h2>Keep store decisions beside the guidance</h2><p>For each adopted procedure record the store-specific rule, rationale, owner, effective date and evidence. Link the actual workflow or contract. Guides provide a starting structure; they cannot know your current queue, approved offer or legal assessment. Review affected decisions when an integration, sender, catalog rule or owner changes.</p></div></section>
  <nav class="container pb-12 flex flex-wrap gap-4" aria-label="Related operating guidance">
    <a class="link" href="/guides/implementation-plan">Implementation plan</a>
    <a class="link" href="/guides/migration">Migration</a>
    <a class="link" href="/guides/flow-collision-prevention">Flow collision prevention</a>
    <a class="link" href="/use-cases">Use-case playbooks</a>
    <a class="link" href="/for">Store-type guides</a>
  </nav>
  <FaqSection faqs={faqs} />
</BaseLayout>
